   "resolution": "fix: Item 9701-5.1-x028 is a past-paper extra (source qid 9701_s23_13_q19) whose option texts were extracted one place out; the answer B is right and stays. In build/work/mcq/overrides.json set, for qid 9701_s23_13_q19: stem = 'For a particular reversible reaction the backward reaction is endothermic. The activation energy of the backward reaction is 160 kJ mol⁻¹. It can be assumed that the backward reaction proceeds by a mechanism that is the exact reverse of the mechanism for the forward reaction. Which statement about the activation energy of the forward reaction is correct?'; options A = 'The activation energy of the forward reaction is equal to −160 kJ mol⁻¹.', B = 'The activation energy of the forward reaction is [greater than] 0 kJ mol⁻¹ but less than +160 kJ mol⁻¹.', C = 'The activation energy of the forward reaction is equal to +160 kJ mol⁻¹.', D = 'The activation energy of the forward reaction is greater than +160 kJ mol⁻¹.'; explanation = 'The backward reaction is endothermic, so the forward reaction is exothermic. Both directions pass over the same energy barrier, so the backward activation energy equals the forward activation energy plus the size of the enthalpy change. The forward activation energy is therefore positive but less than 160 kJ mol⁻¹: B. (The printed option B has lost the words greater than.)'. Also set, for qid 9701_s25_13_q2, only explanation = 'Raising the temperature does not change the energy profile: the activation energy and both enthalpy levels stay the same. More particles have at least the activation energy, so the reaction is faster and the reactant concentration falls more steeply. C shows the unchanged pathway with a steeper curve.' Then run add_past and both gates."
